{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788294293,"nonce":"toUIdkNf3FuA6qM3NaMrPHtPxc8=","message":"COMMENT #1 IS REFUTED, AND ITS OWN CLOSING SENTENCE IS THE PART THAT SURVIVES. Measured on a live bench 2026-09-01 (session `20260901T195344`, `accept/runs/s20-20260901/`) while discharging `20e5cda`'s missing bench run. This touches ONLY the `data.after` half added in #1; bullets 1 and 2 of the body — the clamp echo and the currency row in `buy_value`/`sell_value` — are untouched and still stand.\n\n## `data.after` is CORRECT. There is nothing to fix in it.\n\n#1 hypothesised the mechanism as **forbidden stock**: \"the independent read shows 30 of those 60 are forbidden … forbidden and unreachable stock is invisible to it.\" That is not the mechanism, and the numbers in #1 never fitted it — a forbidden filter over 60 with 30 forbidden gives 30, not the 50 that was observed. 50 + the 10 just bought = 60 is what fits.\n\n**Direct disproof of the forbidden hypothesis, measured today:** `trade-start` reported `colony_silver: 2800` on a map holding 2000 unforbidden silver in the home area and 800 FORBIDDEN silver (two map-scatter stacks at [133,136] and [134,136], `forbidden: true`). The forbidden 800 was counted in full. `RimWorld/TradeUtility.PlayerSellableNow` has no forbidden clause and neither does `RimWorld/Pawn_TraderTracker.ColonyThingsWillingToBuy`.\n\n**The real mechanism is WHERE THE GOODS LAND.**\n\n- `RimWorld/Tradeable.ResolveTrade` hands a buy to `TransferableUtility.TransferNoSplit(thingsTrader, …)`, which walks the trader's stack LIST and calls `GiveSoldThingToPlayer` **once per stack**.\n- `RimWorld/Pawn_TraderTracker.GiveSoldThingToPlayer` places each with `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(thing, toGive.PositionHeld, mapHeld, ThingPlaceMode.Near)` — at **whichever caravan member was carrying that stack**, NOT near the negotiator — then `pawn.GetLord()?.extraForbiddenThings.Add(thing)`.\n- `ColonyThingsWillingToBuy`'s test is `def.category == Item \u0026\u0026 PlayerSellableNow \u0026\u0026 !Position.Fogged \u0026\u0026 (map.areaManager.Home[pos] || IsInAnyStorage()) \u0026\u0026 ReachableForTrade`.\n\nA caravan parked outside the home area satisfies neither `Home[pos]` nor `IsInAnyStorage()`, so bought goods are legitimately not colony stock until somebody hauls them. **Vanilla's own `Dialog_Trade` prints the same optimistic post-deal column**, so the mod is reproducing the game, not diverging from it.\n\n(The `extraForbiddenThings` add does not forbid them to colonists: `RimWorld/ForbidUtility.IsForbidden(Thing, Pawn)` consults `pawn.GetLord()` — the lord of the pawn ASKING — and a colonist has none. It stops the caravan re-collecting what it sold. Both delivered stacks read `forbidden: false`.)\n\n## Three live deals, all correct and all different\n\n| deal | currency line | colony-side delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| paid for components | -360 | **-360** (exact) |\n| sold components | +83 | **0** |\n| sold pemmican | +80 | **69** |\n\nAn OUTFLOW is exact — the stacks are taken FROM colony scope. An INFLOW is neither exact nor all-or-nothing: it is however many carriers happened to stand inside the home area. 69 of 80 is what a partially-parked caravan looks like. **No exact assertion on the colony-side count is possible for an inflow**, which is why `accept/3.5-dialog-verbs.py` now asserts equality on the outflow and a BOUND on the inflow, and proves delivery on the two numbers that are not deal-scoped: the trader's own holdings (972 -\u003e 889, 103 -\u003e 93, exact both times) and an independent whole-map `things {def}` read.\n\n## What is left of #1, restated as a spec rather than a bug\n\n#1's last line was right and is the whole of the remaining work: *\"a number that is correct for what it actually measures, presented as an answer to a different question.\"*\n\n`data.after[].colony_now`, `totals.colony_silver` and `totals.colony_silver_post_deal` are all **deal-scope** counts — \"what the colony could put on this table\" — and the question an agent has after a purchase is \"did it arrive and can my colonists get at it\". Those are different questions and the surface answers only the first, under a name that reads like the second.\n\nProposed, narrowed:\n\n- **Rename or annotate.** `colony_now` keeps its meaning and gains a stated scope (`scope: \"deal\"`, or `tradeable_now`), so it cannot be read as inventory.\n- **Publish the honest second figure beside it.** `map_now` — every stack of the def on the map — plus `at`, the cells the delivery actually landed on, which `GiveSoldThingToPlayer` knows and nothing publishes. \"Your 10 wood is at [83,87], 45 cells away, and needs hauling\" is the answer; \"63\" is not.\n- **Say it once in the verb's own `note`**, the way `trade-cancel`'s `untouched_means` does, so the distinction survives without a reader going to this issue.\n\nAcceptance for that half:\n- A buy from a caravan parked outside the home area publishes a colony-side figure that does not move AND a map-side figure that moves by exactly the bought count, with both scopes named in the envelope.\n- The landing cells are published.\n- Proven on a bench with the caravan outside the home area, since that is the case the numbers diverge in.\n\nBullets 1 and 2 of the body are unaffected by any of this.","files":null}]}